infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Liveness vs readiness: two probes, opposite consequences
  desc Same probe shape — but liveness kills the pod while readiness only reroutes it
  compares
    - label Liveness probe
      children
        - label Liveness = kill switch
          desc Fail -> SIGTERM then SIGKILL, pod restarts as a fresh container
        - label Asks: is my event loop alive?
          desc Cheap in-process check, no I/O to dependencies
        - label Never checks a dependency
          desc One DB blip fails every pod at once -> whole-fleet restart storm
    - label Readiness probe
      children
        - label Readiness = routing switch
          desc Fail -> dropped from Service endpoints, pod is NOT killed
        - label Asks: route traffic here now?
          desc On SIGTERM flip it to 503 first to drain the LB
        - label Reflects real dependencies
          desc DB pool exhausted -> 503 sheds load as correct backpressure
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
